well the sudden closure of a large  wedding dress retailer has left many  brides to be scrambling to find a dress  in time for their big day Alfred Angelo  filed for chapter 7 bankruptcy on Friday  it closed all 61 of its stores just  before two of its most popular wedding  months August and September mega lovers  at an Alfred Angelo store in Cherry Hill  New Jersey to show us how the sudden  collapse is impacting plans for  countless weddings meg my heart goes out  to so many of these women so many be on  a good morning the bankruptcy also  caught many Alfred Angelo employees by  surprise across the country distraught  Brides have been coming to stores like  this one trying to get the dresses  they've paid for or put a deposit down  on many left empty-handed where's my  dress from California do I need to start  looking for another dress to Iowa every  Brides worst nightmare  to Indiana really screwed everybody over  brides felt jilted their wedding dresses  locked behind closed doors  Erin Casey bought her Alfred Angelo  dress last month I loved it it was the  first dress I tried on Casey paid more  than $1,200 for her dream dress  now she's worried she won't wear it down  the aisle in December I've tried calling  the store but it goes straight to  voicemail and voicemail is full in court  papers Alfred Angelo estimates its  assets at ten to fifty million dollars  but says it owes fifty to 100 million to  as many as twenty five thousand  creditors and customers the Florida  based retailer has been in business for  more than eight decades  last Monday its Board of Directors  authorized the chapter 7 bankruptcy  filing the first step towards  liquidating the company it suggests that  they think that there's no way to save  the business at all bankruptcy law  professor Stephen Levin says the brides  with the best chance of getting their  money back are those who already paid  for their dresses those dresses are  arguably theirs and they should be  entitled to them of course whether that  can all be sorted out in time for their  wedding is a big question  some of Alfred Angela's competitors have  stepped in giving away sample dresses or  offering discounts for them to just kind  of drop this news overnight  it's a shame on you moment now brides  who paid for their dresses with a credit  card can ask their banks for their money  back in a statement to customers Alfred  Angelo wrote we deeply apologize for the  inconvenience and hardship resulting  from this event we greatly appreciate  your patience Jeff make thanks very much  can only imagine that's good that other  retailers are jumping in those  discounted prices absolutely
 

